      "message": "lgtm!\n\nI\u0027d find it easier to follow the code if it was spelled out somehere where limits functions are called. The code is hard to follow.\n\nApparently `NormalizeLimits` is call by/for an Adapter after the PhysicalDevice has provided the hardware\u0027s physical limits. `NormalizeLimi`t is a chance to enforce Dawn/WebGPU limits, over and above the hardware\u0027s limits.\n\nThere are so many places limits get affected\n\ndefault limits\nharware/drive limits\nadapter limits\nrequired limits\ndevice limits\n\nLike one idea would be rename NormalizeLimits to NormalizeAdapterLimitsAfterGettingPhysicsalLimits. It might seem silly but it would spell out where in those 5 steps above this function is used, without having to go find where it happens to be documented.\n\nhttps://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/223860 adds `FixupDeviceLimits` (though maybe your review would suggest this should go somewhere else). It\u0027s point is to fix up the limits for the device AFTER the required limits have been validated. Maybe I should rename it to `FixupDeviceLimitsAfterRequiredLimitsHaveBeenValidated`",
